Package unix for Radix (GOOS=radix, ADR 0600). Radix's programs reach
the kernel through its C library, mlibc, never directly, as OpenBSD's
reach theirs: each function calls the library's through a trampoline,
as package syscall does on Radix (ports/go). The C library's POSIX
interface takes Linux's numbers and structures, so the constants and
types are Linux's, generated from mlibc's headers: mkerrors.sh reads
the names from mlibc's source (MLIBC_SRC) rather than running a program
on Radix, and mksyscall.go -libc writes the trampolines. Syscall,
Syscall6, Syscall9, RawSyscall and RawSyscall6 fail with ENOSYS, as
package syscall's do on Radix. Shared files name radix where Radix does
what they do.

go.mod names Go 1.22, the oldest whose language this code builds with,
so that a program whose go.mod names an older Go than 1.26 may take it
in place of any version of the module (ADR 0600).

Regenerate, with the toolchain built (./ob ports) and mlibc's source in
target/ports/work/mlibc/src, in unix/:

    export PATH=$PWD/../../../../out/toolchain/bin:$PATH
    export CC=x86_64-radix-cc MLIBC_SRC=<mlibc source> GOOS=radix GOARCH=amd64
    bash mkerrors.sh | gofmt > zerrors_radix_amd64.go
    GOOS_TARGET=radix GOOS=linux go run mksyscall.go -libc -tags radix,amd64 \
        syscall_radix.go syscall_radix_amd64.go | gofmt > zsyscall_radix_amd64.go
    GOARCH=amd64 go tool cgo -godefs types_radix.go |
        GOOS_TARGET=radix GOOS=linux go run mkpost.go > ztypes_radix_amd64.go
    GOOS=linux go run mkasm.go radix amd64

