+// Radix system calls.
+// Radix's programs reach the kernel through the C library (mlibc), as
+// OpenBSD's do, and its POSIX interface takes Linux's numbers and
+// structures: the constants and types here are Linux's, and each function
+// is the C library's, which the runtime calls on the system stack through
+// a trampoline. Radix has no system call numbers, so Syscall and its
+// relatives fail with ENOSYS.
+// This file is compiled as ordinary Go code,
+// but it is also input to mksyscall,
+// which parses the //sys lines and generates the calls.
+// Note that sometimes we use a lowercase //sys name and wrap
+// it in our own nicer implementation, either here or in
+// syscall_unix.go.
